Causa -> Queries ineficientes, falta de índices ou picos de carga podem elevar o uso da CPU
Regra -> Identificar processos ativos com maior consumo
Verificação -> Execute: SELECT pid, query, cpu_usage FROM pg_stat_activity ORDER BY cpu_usage DESC LIMIT 10;

Causa -> Erro 500 genérico (ambos os cenários possíveis)
Regra -> Diagnóstico exige telemetria específica
Verificação -> 1) Ative tracing completo na API 2) Capture X-Request-Id de falhas 3) Execute: curl -v https://api.pagamentos/v1/transactions/trace/{requestId}

Causa -> Alta latência pode indicar deadlocks, mas sem evidências diretas é apenas uma hipótese.
Regra -> Deadlocks são registrados nos logs do PostgreSQL e visíveis em pg_stat_activity/pg_locks.
Verificação -> Execute imediatamente:
1. SELECT * FROM pg_stat_activity WHERE state = 'active';
2. SELECT blocked_locks.pid AS blocked_pid, blocking_locks.pid AS blocking_pid FROM pg_catalog.pg_locks blocked_locks JOIN pg_catalog.pg_locks blocking_locks ON blocking_locks.locktype = blocked_locks.locktype AND blocking_locks.DATABASE IS NOT DISTINCT FROM blocked_locks.DATABASE AND blocking_locks.relation IS NOT DISTINCT FROM blocked_locks.relation AND blocking_locks.page IS NOT DISTINCT FROM blocked_locks.page AND blocking_locks.tuple IS NOT DISTINCT FROM blocked_locks.tuple AND blocking_locks.virtualxid IS NOT DISTINCT FROM blocked_locks.virtualxid AND blocking_locks.transactionid IS NOT DISTINCT FROM blocked_locks.transactionid AND blocking_locks.classid IS NOT DISTINCT FROM blocked_locks.classid AND blocking_locks.objid IS NOT DISTINCT FROM blocked_locks.objid AND blocking_locks.objsubid IS NOT DISTINCT FROM blocked_locks.objsubid WHERE NOT blocked_locks.granted;
